## What the app screen does

AutoWifi's main screen is where you choose a network mode, configure a connection, select a protocol, save the configuration, and start or stop the service. Labels and layout may vary between app versions; the [Google Play listing](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.gyan.autowifi) has the current app details and screenshots.

| Main-screen control | What it is for |
| --- | --- |
| **Network Mode** | Choose Wi-Fi Mode or Direct Mode. |
| **SSID and password** | Enter a Wi-Fi network or choose one from the scan dialog. Leave the password blank for an open network. |
| **Protocol** | Select SOCKS, VPN, SSH, or Port Forwarding Only. |
| **Save** | Apply and lock the current configuration. |
| **Start / Started** | Start the background service and check its ongoing notification for connection status. |
| **Settings** | Configure service ports, routing preferences, app-split selection, and other options. |
| **Profiles** | Save and switch between connection configurations. |

> **First time here?** Pick a mode, enter the required network or server details, select a protocol, tap **Save**, and then tap **Start**.

